! X resources for this prefix's Wine only: env.sh points XENVIRONMENT here, which overrides the
! desktop's resources (xrdb) for these programs.
!
! Grayscale instead of subpixel (LCD) font antialiasing. With Xft.rgba: rgb (KDE Plasma's default)
! Wine renders text in LCD mode, and GE-Proton11-7's freetype_get_glyph_outline dereferences a NULL
! bitmap for the very wide glyphs of Office's font-preview font (the font list in the ribbon). Wine
! catches the access violation but leaves win32u's font lock held, and Word freezes at its next
! font call.
Xft.rgba: none
